<div class="post-hero"><div class="wrap"><a href="/blog" class="back-link">&larr; Back to Blog</a><div class="post-hero-meta"><span class="post-cat">Health &amp; Wellness</span><span class="post-read">7 min read</span></div><h1>How Adult Family Homes Can Get More Residents Through Google Search</h1><div class="post-author-row"><div class="author-avatar">RF</div><div><strong>Right Framework Team</strong><span>May 10, 2026</span></div></div></div></div>
<div class="post-layout wrap">
  <article class="post-content">
    <p class="post-lead">Families facing the decision of finding the right care home for a loved one start their search on Google. Adult family homes that show up at the right moment — with the right information, tone, and trust signals — fill vacancies faster and attract the families that are the best fit.</p>
    <h2>How Families Search for Care Homes Online</h2>
    <p>The search journey for an adult family home almost always begins with a Google search. Families in King County, Snohomish County, and across the Pacific Northwest are typing queries like "adult family home Seattle," "memory care home Bellevue," "senior care Kirkland WA," and "licensed AFH near Redmond" into Google every single day. They're looking for options they can trust — and the homes that show up in those results get the calls.</p>
    <p>What many adult family home operators don't realize is that the competition for these searches is actually quite manageable compared to many other industries. The families searching for care homes are highly motivated — they're making urgent, important decisions. Being visible in Google at this moment is extraordinarily valuable.</p>
    <h2>Why Your Google Business Profile Is Your #1 Asset</h2>
    <p>Your Google Business Profile is often the first thing a family sees when they search for care home options in your area. A complete, well-maintained profile significantly increases your visibility in local search results and Google Maps.</p>
    <p>Here's what your Google Business Profile needs to be complete:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Category:</strong> "Assisted Living Facility" or "Nursing Home" as your primary category</li>
      <li><strong>Photos:</strong> At minimum, exterior photos, living areas, dining spaces, garden or outdoor areas, and common rooms — 20+ high-quality images</li>
      <li><strong>Description:</strong> 750 characters describing your care philosophy, specializations (memory care, hospice support, specific medical needs), and the community you serve</li>
      <li><strong>Reviews:</strong> Actively request reviews from families of current and past residents. Respond thoughtfully to every review.</li>
      <li><strong>Attributes:</strong> Mark all applicable accessibility features, language services, and specialty care options</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>What Families Look for on Your Website</h2>
    <p>Once a family clicks through to your website, what they find in the next 30 seconds determines whether they call you or go back and click on the next result. Families evaluating adult family homes are looking for very specific information:</p>
    <h3>Licensing and credentials</h3>
    <p>Your Washington State AFH license number should be visible on your homepage. Families want immediate confirmation that you're legitimate and regulated. If you have additional certifications, specialized training, or affiliations with care associations, display these prominently.</p>
    <h3>Staff information</h3>
    <p>Families are trusting you with someone they love. Brief staff bios, caregiving philosophy, training backgrounds, and tenure information all humanize your home and build the personal connection that leads to inquiry calls. A photo and a few sentences about the primary caregiver makes an enormous difference in conversion.</p>
    <h3>Room and amenity photos</h3>
    <p>Clear, warm, well-lit photos of your home — bedrooms, common areas, the garden, the dining setup — answer the most important visual question families have before they visit. Homes with strong photography consistently get more inquiries than those with limited or poor-quality images.</p>
    <h3>Clear contact and tour request form</h3>
    <p>Your contact form should make it effortless for a family to reach you. Ask for name, phone, email, and a brief description of their loved one's needs. A "Request a Tour" button that's visible without scrolling dramatically increases inquiry conversions.</p>
    <h2>Local SEO Keywords for Adult Family Homes</h2>
    <p>The most effective SEO strategy for adult family homes focuses on the intersection of location and care type. Target keyword combinations like:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>"Adult family home Seattle WA"</li>
      <li>"Licensed memory care home Bellevue"</li>
      <li>"Senior care home Kirkland"</li>
      <li>"AFH with dementia care near Redmond"</li>
      <li>"Adult family home South King County"</li>
      <li>"Affordable assisted living Bothell WA"</li>
    </ul>
    <p>These longer, more specific keyword phrases have lower search volume than generic terms but much higher conversion rates — the families searching these specific queries are further along in their decision process and more likely to call.</p>
    <h2>Building Trust Through Content</h2>
    <p>A blog or resources section on your website serves two purposes: it gives Google fresh, relevant content to index (which helps your rankings), and it positions your home as a knowledgeable, caring resource for families navigating a difficult process.</p>
    <p>Helpful content topics for adult family homes include: "What is the difference between an adult family home and an assisted living facility?", "How to evaluate an adult family home in Washington State," "What to look for when visiting a potential care home," and "Understanding Washington State AFH licensing requirements." Each of these answers real questions families are searching for.</p>
    <h2>The Difference a Professional Website Makes</h2>
    <p>Consider two adult family homes serving the same neighborhoods in the Eastside. One has a professional website with a warm design, clear licensing information, staff bios, beautiful photography of the home, a tour request form, and blog content that answers common family questions. The other has a simple listing on a care directory with minimal information.</p>
    <p>The first home gets consistent inquiry calls from families who have already done their research, are largely pre-qualified, and feel a connection before they've even visited. The second home waits for referrals and word of mouth. The difference in occupancy rates over 12 months is significant — and it's entirely driven by online presence.</p>
    <h2>Getting Started</h2>
    <p>If your adult family home doesn't have a professional website, or if your current site isn't generating inquiries, the path forward is clear. A well-designed website, an optimized Google Business Profile, and a consistent approach to local SEO keywords can meaningfully change your occupancy rates within 3–6 months.</p>
    <p>At Right Framework, we understand the unique trust requirements of the healthcare and care home space. We build websites that communicate warmth, credibility, and competence — the three things families need to feel before they make an inquiry call. If you'd like to talk about what's possible for your home, we offer a free consultation with no obligation.</p>
    <div class="faq-section">
      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>How do families search for adult family homes in Seattle?</h3>
        <p>Most families start with Google searches like "adult family home Seattle" or "memory care home near me." They then visit 3–5 websites before contacting anyone, making your website's first impression critically important.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>What should an adult family home website include?</h3>
        <p>Photos of the home and common spaces, caregiver bios, services offered, licensing information, resident capacity, a warm about section, and a clear contact form. Trust signals matter enormously in this space.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>How can an adult family home rank higher on Google in Seattle?</h3>
        <p>Optimize your Google Business Profile with accurate details and recent photos. Use neighborhood-specific keywords on your website. Ask families to leave Google reviews. Publish helpful content about senior care.</p>
      </div>
